--- STEP A: alpha band width vs march step ---
A fan of rays sweeps across the silhouette; for each stride the 10-90% rise of accumulated alpha is measured in world blocks at the
tangent point, then converted to capture pixels. 'phase' means a uniform random origin offset over one stride, which is what production's
blue-noise jitter does. If the band collapses with the stride the cause is the march; if it converges, the cause is the field.
