--- STEP C: the grazing-chord floor ---
Even a perfectly sharp density boundary produces a soft silhouette, because the chord through a convex body grows as sqrt(depth) at the
tangent. This is that floor for the measured body radius, and it is the width no sampling change can go below.
hard-sphere 10%-90% alpha band|0.475 blocks|1.533 px
  (R=166.0, sigma=0.09171/block, tangent distance 228.2)

--- STEP D: band vs camera distance ---
The captured frames show the boundary band constant in WORLD blocks and shrinking as 1/distance in PIXELS. If this model reproduces that
trend it is describing the same boundary the renderer draws, which is what licenses the STEP A conclusion.
